<reference id="_Toc235450349" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — Paragraph with mixed inline character styles</title>
   <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>inline</keyword>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>HTML</keyword>
        <keyword>Paragraph</keyword>
        <keyword>mixed</keyword>
        <keyword>character</keyword>
        <indexterm>inline</indexterm>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
        <indexterm>HTML</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
    <p>Consider an HTML <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element that contains a mix of bold, italic, and monospace formatting applied to individual words or phrases within the same paragraph. The converter maps each recognized inline HTML element to the corresponding DITA inline element within the same <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Paragraph with mixed inline character styles</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;p>Press &lt;strong>OK&lt;/strong> to save, or run &lt;code>setup.sh&lt;/code> using &lt;em>administrator&lt;/em> privileges.&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;p>Press &lt;b>OK&lt;/b> to save, or run &lt;codeph>setup.sh&lt;/codeph> using &lt;i>administrator&lt;/i> privileges.&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
        <p>
            <b>Result:</b> The converter preserves all inline formatting within a single <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element. Each recognized inline HTML element is mapped to its DITA equivalent:</p>
         <ul id="ul_09045107">
            <li>
               <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> → <codeph>&lt;b&gt;</codeph>,</li>
            <li>
               <codeph>&lt;em&gt;</codeph> → <codeph>&lt;i&gt;</codeph>,</li>
            <li>
               <codeph>&lt;code&gt;</codeph> → <codeph>&lt;codeph&gt;</codeph>.</li>
         </ul><p>For a full list of inline element mappings, see the <xref href="../inline_formatting/inline_formatting.dita" format="dita">Inline Formatting</xref> section.</p>
  </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
